                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A separate strand of the microstructure literature asks not how much information trading contains, but where that information is impounded into price when a security trades across multiple venues or related instruments. Hasbrouck (1995) develops the information-share methodology, decomposing the innovation in a security's common efficient price into the proportional contributions of each market in which it trades. While our setting is single-market rather than multi-market, the underlying logic is directly relevant: just",
